---
import { url } from "../../lib/url";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { changelog, libraries, manualPath, repoTree, site, version } from "../../data/site";
---

<Base title="Libraries">
	<section class="header">
		<div class="container">
			<h1>Libraries</h1>
			<p class="lead">
				Besides research prototypes, Bismuth contains libraries that are ready for building local-first applications. They
				are published separately and can be used individually, on the JVM, in the browser via Scala.js, and natively via Scala Native (group id <code>de.tu-darmstadt.stg</code>). We document the{" "}
				<b>RDTs</b> (algebraic replicated data types) and <b>Reactives</b> libraries with a hands-on manual each, and all
				libraries with generated API documentation (Scaladoc). To build the code yourself, see{" "}
				<a href="#development">working with the repository</a> below.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
	<section class="section bg-light">
		<div class="container grid">
			{
				libraries.map((l) => (
					<div class="lib-card">
						<h3>{l.title}</h3>
						<p>{l.summary}</p>
						<div class="lib-links">
							{l.manual ? (
								<a class="lib-link primary" href={url(manualPath(l.manual))}>
									<span>Manual</span>
									<small>{l.manual}</small>
								</a>
							) : (
								<span class="lib-link disabled">
									<span>Manual</span>
									<small>not yet available</small>
								</span>
							)}
							<div class="lib-link">
								<span>Scaladoc</span>
								<small class="platforms">
									{l.scaladoc.map((d) => <a href={d.href}>{d.platform} ↗</a>)}
								</small>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				))
			}
		</div>
		<div class="container">
			<div class="deps">
				<h3>Using the libraries</h3>
				<p>
					The current version is {version}. See the <a href={url(manualPath(changelog))}>changelog</a> for what changed.
				</p>
				<input type="radio" name="dep-tool" id="dep-sbt" checked />
				<label for="dep-sbt">sbt</label>
				<input type="radio" name="dep-tool" id="dep-scala-cli" />
				<label for="dep-scala-cli">scala-cli</label>
				<input type="radio" name="dep-tool" id="dep-mill" />
				<label for="dep-mill">mill</label>
				<pre class="dep-sbt"><code>{`libraryDependencies += "de.tu-darmstadt.stg" %% "rdts" % "${version}"
libraryDependencies += "de.tu-darmstadt.stg" %% "reactives" % "${version}"
libraryDependencies += "de.tu-darmstadt.stg" %% "channels" % "${version}"`}</code></pre>
				<pre class="dep-scala-cli"><code>{`//> using dep de.tu-darmstadt.stg::rdts::${version}
//> using dep de.tu-darmstadt.stg::reactives::${version}
//> using dep de.tu-darmstadt.stg::channels::${version}`}</code></pre>
				<pre class="dep-mill"><code>{`def mvnDeps = Seq(
  mvn"de.tu-darmstadt.stg::rdts::${version}",
  mvn"de.tu-darmstadt.stg::reactives::${version}",
  mvn"de.tu-darmstadt.stg::channels::${version}"
)`}</code></pre>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
	<section class="section" id="development">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Working with the repository</h2>
			<p class="lead">
				Bismuth is a single <a href="https://www.scala-sbt.org/">sbt</a> build with many modules. You rarely need all of
				them, so compile and test only the module you work on.
			</p>

			<ol class="steps">
				<li>
					<h3>Install sbt</h3>
					<p>
						Follow the <a href="https://www.scala-sbt.org/download/">official install instructions</a>. You also need
						Java 21 or newer. Compile everything once to check that it works.
					</p>
					<pre><code>sbt compile</code></pre>
				</li>
				<li>
					<h3>Compile and test</h3>
					<p>
						Prefix a command with the module name, and use <code>projects</code> to list all modules. The JVM variant has no suffix, the others end in <code>JS</code>{" "}
						or <code>Native</code>.
					</p>
					<pre><code>sbt 'rdts/compile'
sbt 'reactivesJS/test'</code></pre>
					<p class="note">Tests of Scala.js modules need npm packages. Run <code>npm install</code> once in the project root.</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="hint">
				The <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/Justfile`}>Justfile</a> collects further commands, for example to run the
				web demos.
			</p>

			<h3 class="subhead">IDE setup</h3>
			<p>Both IntelliJ and Metals generally work well with the project. Start sbt once from the command line before importing.</p>
			<div class="grid ide">
				<div class="ide-card">
					<h4><a href="https://www.jetbrains.com/help/idea/get-started-with-scala.html">IntelliJ</a> with the Scala plugin</h4>
					<p>
						Open the root folder and use the normal sbt import. Alternatively, choose <b>BSP</b> so IntelliJ compiles and tests
						through sbt. The BSP importer drops some dependencies of shared test sources (<a href="https://youtrack.jetbrains.com/issue/SCL-23703">SCL-23703</a>).
						To fix that, close the project after each import and run:
					</p>
					<pre><code>just intellij-bsp-import-fix</code></pre>
				</div>
				<div class="ide-card">
					<h4><a href="https://scalameta.org/metals/">Metals</a> language server</h4>
					<p>
						Works with VS Code and many other editors. Metals can also use{" "}
						<a href="https://scalameta.org/metals/docs/build-tools/sbt/#sbt-build-server">sbt as BSP server</a>, but the
						default import is usually fine.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<h3 class="subhead">Repository layout</h3>
			<ul class="tree">
				{
					repoTree.map((e) => (
						<li class:list={{ dim: e.dim }}>
							<div class="tree-row">
								<code class="tree-name">{e.name}</code>
								<span class="tree-summary">
									{e.summary}
									{e.sbt && <span class="tree-sbt">{e.sbt.map((p) => <code>{p}</code>)}</span>}
								</span>
							</div>
							{e.children && (
								<ul>
									{e.children.map((c) => (
										<li class:list={{ dim: c.dim }}>
											<div class="tree-row">
												<code class="tree-name">{c.name}</code>
												<span class="tree-summary">
													{c.summary}
													{c.sbt && <span class="tree-sbt">{c.sbt.map((p) => <code>{p}</code>)}</span>}
												</span>
											</div>
										</li>
									))}
								</ul>
							)}
						</li>
					))
				}
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section bg-indigo">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Questions?</h2>
			<p class="lead">
				Join our matrix channel if you run into problems or want to coordinate larger changes. Anyone can join, but
				messages are only visible to members.
			</p>
			<div class="buttons">
				<a class="hero" href="https://matrix.to/#/#difosys:matrix.tu-darmstadt.de">Join the chat</a>
				<a class="hero secondary" href="https://element.matrix.tu-darmstadt.de/#/room/#difosys:matrix.tu-darmstadt.de">Join the chat with TU-ID</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
